## 7. Error Handling & Validation

### 7.1 Error Handling Patterns
- Prioritize error handling and edge cases
- Use early returns for error conditions
- Implement guard clauses to handle preconditions and invalid states early
- Use custom error types for consistent error handling
- Implement proper error boundaries in React
- **No Console Logging**: Do not use `console.log`, `console.warn`, `console.error`, or any other console methods in production code. Use proper logging libraries or error tracking services instead 

### 7.2 Validation
- Implement user input validation on both client and server
- Use type-safe validation libraries (e.g., Zod) for runtime validation
- Validate data at API boundaries

